Try to ID some scrolls of enchant weapon ASAP, and get holy water.
Blessing and enchanting your arrows will make them last longer. Even
if sticking to daggers, the enchantment will help you do a lot more
damage.

If you're an elf, your starting bow and arrow get you an extra shot
per turn, so you might want to use them, but don't use them regularly
until you can bless the +2 ones and get a luckstone.

Use a stack of dagers for most attacks, but switch to your +2 arrows
for emergencies. Assuming of course that your skill is the same.
Number fired per turn increases with skill.

Other than that you should be ok already. Speed boots will let you run
enough to fire without being hit.

Your AC should be fine with just the GDSM. For a ranger, the best
defense is to kill them before they get close to you. Rangers aren't
meant to be a melee role either.

